  "_comment": "AREF-001 DRAFT resource-effect catalogue. NOT a shipped artefact: this file lives under specs/ and is not loaded by any code. It exists so that the catalogue design (AREF-001 D-06) can be reviewed against real rule IDs before any of it is implemented. Coverage: the 31 Python sink rules in actenon_scan/rules/default_rules.json, the 9 rule IDs emitted by actenon_scan/detectors/typescript.py, and the 9 emitted by actenon_scan/detectors/go.py (keyed after D-14 normalisation, which strips the -GO suffix). NO ENTRY HAS STATUS 'frozen'. That is deliberate and is the catalogue's main honest statement: promoting an entry from draft to frozen asserts that its declared selector location is correct on real call sites, and that assertion requires the REI-001 measurement which is not accessible (see 01-EVIDENCE-AVAILABILITY.md and blocked decision B-03). KEYWORD POLICY: arg_keywords are restricted to lowercase, vendor-neutral parameter names. No vendor-specific keyword (CamelCase SDK parameter names, provider-branded fields) appears anywhere in this file, because the task prohibits provider-specific rules and because a vendor keyword list in a data file is a provider-specific rule wearing a different hat. The NET-EGRESS keyword set is copied verbatim from that rule's own escalate_when.arg_keywords in default_rules.json, so it introduces nothing new.",
